SPDX identifier: LicenseRef-Fogmare-Mod-License-1.0


Hi! We are Fogmare Motions, a small studio that makes Minecraft mods. We want
people to have fun with our mods, build on them and make cool stuff for them.
We just don't want our work copied, resold, or turned into someone else's
project without us knowing. This license tries to say exactly that, in plain
words.


THE SHORT VERSION

This part is a friendly summary. The numbered sections below are the actual
rules.

You can, without asking us:

- Play the mod, record it, stream it, and earn money from your videos.
- Run it on any server, including servers with donations.
- Put it in free modpacks, as long as the mod is downloaded from its official
  page.
- Make resource packs, data packs, shader tweaks, translations, configs,
  scripts and addons for it, and share them however you like.
- Read the source code, learn from it, and send us fixes.

You need our permission to:

- Put the mod in anything paid, paywalled or exclusive.
- Re-upload the mod anywhere else.
- Release your own edited version, fork or rewrite of it.
- Port it to Bedrock Edition, another game, or a loader or version we don't
  support.
- Copy our code, textures, sounds or other files into your own project.

When in doubt, just ask. We usually answer.


1. WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS

1.1. "The Mod" means the Minecraft mod this license file comes with: its source
code, compiled files (jar), textures, icons, models, sounds, shaders,
animations, cutscenes, written text and dialogue, translations we made, and its
name and logo.

1.2. "We", "us" and "the Studio" mean Fogmare Motions (also called Fogmare),
the creator and copyright holder of the Mod.

1.3. "You" means anyone who downloads, uses, or does anything with the Mod.

1.4. This license applies to every version of the Mod that is released with
this file. Older versions that were released under a different license stay
under that license.

1.5. Anything not clearly allowed in this license is not allowed without our
written permission.


2. USING THE MOD

2.1. You may download, install and play the Mod for free, in single player or
multiplayer.

2.2. You may install the Mod on any server, public or private, including
servers that accept donations or sell ranks, as long as you do not charge
people for access to the Mod itself or lock its features behind a payment.

2.3. You may make videos, streams, screenshots, reviews, guides and wiki pages
about the Mod, and you may monetize them. A link to the Mod's official page is
appreciated, but not required.


3. MODPACKS

3.1. You may include the Mod in any free modpack without asking us, as long as:

- the Mod is downloaded from its official page (Modrinth or CurseForge), for
  example through the platform's normal modpack system;
- you do not change the Mod's jar file (changing its config files is fine);
- you do not claim the Mod as your own.

3.2. Rewards that Modrinth or CurseForge pay to modpack authors do not make a
modpack "paid". A pack that is free to download on those platforms counts as
free.

3.3. You need our written permission to include the Mod in:

- a modpack that costs money, or that is only available to paying people
  (Patreon, Boosty, early access, donor-only, and so on);
- a modpack or launcher that ships the Mod's jar file itself instead of
  downloading it from the official page;
- any product, service or server package that you sell.


4. MAKING THINGS FOR THE MOD

4.1. You may create and share, under any license you like, and without asking
us:

- resource packs that change the Mod's textures, models, sounds, text,
  dialogue or translations;
- data packs, tags, configs and presets;
- scripts for scripting mods (such as KubeJS);
- content packs made for the Mod's own features (for example skin packs,
  scenario packs or custom cutscene lines);
- translations into other languages;
- shader packs or shader settings that support the Mod;
- addons and compatibility mods that work with the Mod through its public API,
  events, or other mod-loading tools (for example mixins).

4.2. These are your own creations, with a few simple rules:

- they must not contain the Mod's code, jar, or original files, except where
  you replace them with your own versions or need a tiny piece just to connect
  to the API;
- they must require players to get the Mod separately, from its official page;
- they must not look like official parts of the Mod. A name like "Something
  Addon for (Mod name)" is fine. Using our logo or pretending we made it is
  not.

4.3. Using the Mod's public API is always free and does not require permission,
including for addons you plan to sell. Selling an addon still must not mean
selling or paywalling the Mod itself.


5. THE SOURCE CODE

5.1. You may read the Mod's source code, learn from it, and talk about it.

5.2. You may fork the repository on GitHub, or decompile the Mod, only to:

- study how it works;
- find bugs and fix compatibility problems;
- prepare changes that you send back to us (pull requests).

5.3. You may change the Mod for your own private use. You may not share those
changed versions with others without our permission.

5.4. Learning from our code is fine. Copying it into your own project is not,
unless we say yes.


6. WHAT NEEDS OUR WRITTEN PERMISSION

Without our written permission, you may not:

6.1. Sell the Mod, or put it in any paid, paywalled or exclusive product,
modpack or service (see section 3.3).

6.2. Re-upload or mirror the Mod or its files on any website, launcher or
storage other than its official pages.

6.3. Release a modified version of the Mod, a fork, a "fixed" or "optimized"
build, or a rewrite of it for your own modpack or project.

6.4. Port the Mod to Minecraft: Bedrock Edition, any other game, or any mod
loader or Minecraft version that we don't officially support. This includes
ports made using the Mod's code, assets or name, and projects presented as a
version, port or remake of the Mod.

6.5. Reuse the Mod's code, textures, icons, models, sounds, animations,
cutscenes or text in another project.

6.6. Use the Mod's name, the Studio's name or their logos to promote your own
product, or in a way that makes people think we made or support it.

6.7. Claim the Mod, or any part of it, as your own work.


7. ASKING FOR PERMISSION

7.1. Permission only counts if we give it to you in writing. A message from
Fogmare Motions on Discord or by email is enough.

7.2. Permission is given only to the person or team we gave it to, only for
what we agreed to, and can come with conditions. You can't pass it on to
someone else.

7.3. We are allowed to say no.


8. IF YOU SEND US CONTRIBUTIONS

8.1. If you send us code, art, translations, fixes or other changes (for
example a pull request), you still own your work, but you give Fogmare Motions
a permanent, free, worldwide right to use, change, include and distribute it as
part of the Mod or our other projects, under any license, including
commercially.

8.2. By sending a contribution, you confirm that it is your own work, or that
you have the right to give it to us.


9. THINGS THAT ARE NOT OURS

9.1. Minecraft is owned by Mojang Studios and Microsoft. The Mod is not an
official Minecraft product and is not approved by or associated with Mojang or
Microsoft. Your use of Minecraft is also covered by Mojang's own terms.

9.2. Libraries and mods that the Mod depends on keep their own licenses.

9.3. Skins, textures, packs and other files that players create or load into
the Mod belong to whoever made them. This license does not cover them.


10. BREAKING THE RULES

10.1. If you break this license, your permissions under it end automatically.

10.2. If you fix the problem within 30 days after we tell you about it, your
permissions come back, unless you have broken the license before.

10.3. We may ask websites and platforms to remove content that breaks this
license.


11. NO WARRANTY

The Mod is provided "as is", without any warranty. We are not responsible for
any damage, lost worlds, crashes or other problems caused by using it. Back up
your worlds.


12. OTHER THINGS

12.1. We may change this license for future versions of the Mod. Each version
is covered by the license it was released with.

12.2. If any part of this license can't be enforced where you live, the rest
of it still applies.

12.3. The short version at the top is only a summary. If it and the numbered
sections ever disagree, the numbered sections win.

Thanks for reading this far. Have fun with the mod!

Fogmare Motions
